    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0381" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Y2/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-02T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3857. Your 4929, January 26, 11 a.m., and 4973, January 31, 9 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d245-f1"/> You are instructed to take up the matter personally with
                    Zimmermann or Hollweg and insist upon being informed immediately whether any
                    Americans are among the prisoners brought in on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarrowdale:</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d245-f2"/> Let nothing be undone to
                    determine this fact at <pb facs="0382" n="210" xml:id="pg210"/> the earliest
                    moment. If there are Americans among the prisoners, emphatically, vigorously
                    insist both formally and in person upon their release, as there is no authority
                    in law for the imprisonment of neutrals taken on board enemy merchantmen unless
                    the vessel takes part in hostilities. See rules laid down in Hague Convention
                    XI.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="1" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram of Jan. 31 not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="2" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p>The names of the American citizens on the <hi rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale</hi>
                    were given to Ambassador Gerard by the German Foreign Office Feb. 1, and the
                    telegram containing them reached the Department Feb. 2 at 6 p.m. (File No.
                    763.72111Y2/10).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
